  "$comment": "Mission 1.82 §9. The bounded CPV vocabulary slice: exactly the concepts the frozen lookup universe names, and nothing else. Each label came back from one first-party GET against the Publications Office authority register, in RDF/XML, with the raw response hashed at retrieval. No label is recalled, none is inferred from a neighbouring code, no third-party CPV table was consulted, and the complete CPV vocabulary is deliberately NOT copied into this repository.\n\nTHE LABEL IS DISPLAY METADATA, NEVER IDENTITY. A subject is keyed on its code; the label says what the code means. Renaming or translating a label creates no subject.",
