  "present_in_held_population_but_outside_the_frozen_universe": {
    "codes": {
      "9221": 3,
      "9232": 4,
      "9237": 8
    },
    "level": "class",
    "why": "the freeze took the codes that FORM a cohort under the production membership rule at grain 4, not every code PRESENT on a held notice. These three appear only on notices that also carry another class code, so under C4_REFUSE_AMBIGUOUS_NOTICE they form no cohort at grain 4 and can be no candidate at that grain",
    "labels_retrieved": false,
    "why_not_retrieved": "they are outside the frozen universe, and the freeze is what stops a label from changing which codes get looked up. Widening it after labels had been read would be that move with a structural excuse. Recorded here instead, with the counts, so the gap is visible; a future mission that changes the membership model must re-freeze and look them up",
    "candidate_impact": "NONE: no cohort, no packet, no candidate at grain 4"
  },
